<item><title>Malawi’s plastic waste reaches 75,000 tonnes a year, report estimates</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-plastic-waste-reaches-75-000-tonnes-a-year-report-ea7beb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-plastic-waste-reaches-75-000-tonnes-a-year-report-ea7beb/</guid><category>Malawi</category><description>A 2021 estimate put about 80% of the country’s plastic waste in single-use plastics, amid concern over disposal along the Lilongwe-Kasungu road.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:21:49 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mw.jpg" length="31502" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mw.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
